        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136926683?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The example code block <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Working_with_objects#objects_and_properties:~:text=There%20is%20no,result%3B%0A%7D\" rel=\"nofollow\">here</a> lists all the inherited properties, regardless whether they are enumerable or not. But the provided description ambiguously says that it lists \"non-enumerable\" properties. And the function name was made more descriptive in this commit.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I was confused at this thing for a moment, I don't want others to be in the same situation. Simple.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
