        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Added details about the elements included in the HTMLFormControlsCollection.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The elements IDL attribute must return an <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-dom-interfaces.html#htmlformcontrolscollection\" rel=\"nofollow\">HTMLFormControlsCollection</a> rooted at the <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#the-form-element\" rel=\"nofollow\">form</a> element's <a href=\"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-root\" rel=\"nofollow\">root</a>, whose filter matches <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#category-listed\" rel=\"nofollow\">listed elements</a> whose <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#form-owner\" rel=\"nofollow\">form owner</a> is the <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#the-form-element\" rel=\"nofollow\">form</a> element, with the exception of <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#the-input-element\" rel=\"nofollow\">input</a> elements whose <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#attr-input-type\" rel=\"nofollow\">type</a> attribute is in the <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#image-button-state-(type=image)\" rel=\"nofollow\">Image Button</a> state, which must, for historical reasons, be excluded from this particular collection.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">related to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3327682986\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40760\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40760/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40760\">#40760</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40841",
            "title": "Enhance HTMLFormControlsCollection description",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-26T14:51:25.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-22T10:01:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Documents that change is made in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1960011\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1960011</a> Filter tabs.onUpdated events by cookieStoreId including a release note and update to the API documentation.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related BCD changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3344085777\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27643\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27643/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27643\">mdn/browser-compat-data#27643</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40838",
            "title": "Bug-1960011 filter tabs.onUpdated results by cookieStoreId",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-26T03:14:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-22T02:51:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 139 updates the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCEncodedAudioFrame/getMetadata\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">RTCEncodedAudioFrame.getMetadata()</code></a> method so that the <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/webrtc-encoded-transform/#dom-rtcencodedaudioframemetadata-audiolevel\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">audioLevel</code></a> property is available in its return object. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5206106602995712\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5206106602995712</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds content for this new return property.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40835",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document RTCEncodedAudioFrame.getMetadata() audioLevel return property",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-27T12:12:49.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-21T19:16:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64606917?u=81c9cbe74db9c6157ba5faf194952f589e6a755f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds enterprise focused guidance note to the storage.managed API documentation clarifying administrative control and proper extension behavior patterns.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Resolves widespread confusion about enterprise policy implementation in WebExtensions. Many developers incorrectly assume managed storage should be user-editable, leading to   disagreements and improper implementations. This note provides authoritative guidance that managed storage is administrator-controlled and read-only, helping developers build compliant enterprise extensions.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>References Mozilla's Enterprise Policy templates: <a href=\"https://mozilla.github.io/policy-templates/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mozilla.github.io/policy-templates/</a></li>\n<li>Aligns with Firefox Enterprise Policy <code class=\"notranslate\">3rdparty</code> documentation</li>\n<li>Provides clear fallback patterns for extensions when managed keys are absent</li>\n<li>Establishes that administrators control changes through native manifests or enterprise policies</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #40018.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3165706748\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40018\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40018/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40018\">#40018</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40833",
            "title": "Add enterprise-focused guidance note for storage.managed API",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-26T16:54:49.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-21T17:33:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ihassansattar",
                "url": "https://github.com/ihassansattar"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR addresses the feedback originally posted by <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/carlosjeurissen/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/carlosjeurissen\">@carlosjeurissen</a> in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2819768304\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/25808\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/25808/hovercard?comment_id=2627793381&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/25808#issuecomment-2627793381\">mdn/browser-compat-data#25808 (comment)</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/rebloor/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/rebloor\">@rebloor</a> can we add a note stating Firefox does not support generating a <code class=\"notranslate\">service_worker</code> based in the <code class=\"notranslate\">scripts</code> key? This is something currently only supported by Apple.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1649521778\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/25808\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/25808/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/25808\">#25808</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1930334\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bugzilla 1930334: Implement background.preferred_environment</a></li>\n<li>Supersede  <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2905812030\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26164\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26164/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/26164#top\">mdn/browser-compat-data#26164 (comment)</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40825",
            "title": "Clarify auto-generation of background service worker in Safari",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-21T23:51:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-20T23:25:19.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43580235?u=cae42d5a371dd041072ce6d85a1808de05535be8&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Using <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;</code> inside <code class=\"notranslate\">@scope</code> changes according to spec updates (and relation to <code class=\"notranslate\">:scope</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This makes <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp; &amp;</code> redundant as far as I can see. The explainer has good context and I hope I've conveyed that in these changes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Explainer:</strong> <a href=\"https://css.oddbird.net/scope/parent-selector/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://css.oddbird.net/scope/parent-selector/</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Bugs</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1975531\" rel=\"nofollow\">Change <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;</code> behaviour inside <code class=\"notranslate\">@scope</code> block as per spec resolution</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Parent issue <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3249101586\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40481\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40481/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40481\">#40481</a></li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> relnote <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3337599065\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40809\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40809/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40809\">#40809</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40814",
            "title": "docs(Fx142): css ampersand in at-scope content and `:scope`",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-27T09:04:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-20T12:50:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "bsmth",
